Per-run procedure (a scratch script, run.sh, not committed, ran these commands in this order; the procedure of ../2026-09-14-recall-one-factor/run.log)
  1. New shell via env -i HOME PATH; cd <project>; set -a; source .env; set +a; export SERVER_PORT=8081 INTEGRATION_ACCESS_TOKEN=<42-character random hex token,
     openssl rand -hex 21, not recorded> plus the run's variables; env | grep -E '^(RAG_[A-Z0-9_]*|RECOMMENDATION_ENABLED|OUTCOMES_ENABLED|IBKR_ENABLED|
     WATCHLIST_ENABLED|SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE|SERVER_PORT)=' printed (per run below); lsof on 8081 -> 0 listeners before every start.
  2. CPU sharing wait: ps -ax -o pid=,args= filtered on surefire|spring-boot:run|StockRecommendationEngineApplication, excluding this run's own mvnw and
     application pids; poll every 30 s, up to 30 minutes; before the app start and before the evaluate call.
  3. nohup ./mvnw -q -o spring-boot:run > app.log 2>&1 &; wait for "Started StockRecommendationEngineApplication"; the "Cross-encoder loaded" line (model path,
     maxLength, batchSize, scoring) confirmed before evaluating.
  4. Warm-up: curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/rag/retrieve -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -H 'Content-Type: application/json'
       -d '{"ticker":"NVDA","query":"What was NVIDIA gross margin in fiscal 2026?","rerank":true}'; its "Reranking filing candidates" line (candidates, timeoutMs)
     confirmed before evaluating.
  5. CPU sharing wait, sysctl -n vm.loadavg, curl --max-time 3600 -X POST "http://localhost:8081/api/rag/evaluate?rerank=true&trace=true" -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
     (one evaluate call per run).
  6. curl GET /api/rag/evaluate/<id> and GET /api/rag/evaluate/<id>/evidence with the run's model still loaded (HTTP status and bytes below).
  7. docker exec -i trading-postgres sh -c 'psql -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -tA -c "select row_to_json(e) from retrieval_evaluations e where id = <id>"'
     -> snapshot-<id>-<run>.json (the single output line with its newline, unaltered).
  8. evidence-<id>.json: the fetched evidence body with whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF) outside JSON strings removed, one line plus a newline; a scratch script parsed
     both texts with every number and constant kept as its written text and printed parses_equal_numbers_as_written=True for each.
  9. grep -E 'Cross-encoder scoring completed|Reranking failed|Retrieval evaluation stored|WARN|ERROR' app.log -> scoring-<id>.txt (its WARNING lines are the JVM's
     startup notices).
  10. Stop: kill the port-8081 listener JVM by pid; 5 s later the mvnw pid if alive; pkill -f spring-boot:run; then lsof on 8081, both pids, and pgrep -f spring-boot:run.

